new file mode 100644
index 0000000000..259983e521
--- /dev/null
+++ b/vllm/third_party/sparkring_mesh_owner/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,161 @@
+# Isolated mesh owner exchange
+
+This package implements one bounded operation: equal-size, four-rank owner
+all-to-all on the existing managed Spark mesh. It allocates its own pinned
+region, CUDA counters, proxy thread, registered MRs and six outgoing QPs per
+rank. It does not install routes/markers, reuse serving slots, or modify any
+running model. The package can be imported as `mesh_owner` or nested under a
+larger package; there is no B12X Python dependency.
+
+```python
+from mesh_owner import MeshOwnerAllToAll, API_VERSION
+
+transport = MeshOwnerAllToAll(
+    exchange_group=gloo_group,  # four ranks, same rank ordering as input owners
+    device="cuda:0",
+    max_input_bytes=32 * 1024 * 1024,
+)
+transport.prepare()  # compile the byte-copy kernel before graph capture
+received = transport.all_to_all(packed, out=received)
+torch.cuda.synchronize()
+transport.check_health()
+# Coordinate final use across ranks before closing their registered regions.
+transport.close()
+```
+
+`OwnerAllToAll` is an alias. `from_exchange_group(...)` and
+`from_process_group(process_group=...)` are alternate constructors.
+`max_size` and `max_gather_bytes` are accepted capacity aliases; the largest
+explicit capacity wins, or 16 MiB is used when none is supplied. Every capacity
+must be a multiple of 64 in `[64, 2147483584]`. Only `world_size=4`,
+`threads=512`, `blocks=8`, two paths per peer and GID index 3 are admitted.
+
+## Tensor and wire contract
+
+For input `x` with `R` rows on source `s`, destination `d` receives
+`x[d * R/4 : (d+1) * R/4]`. Output on rank `d` has the same shape and dtype as
+its input, with these quarters concatenated in source-rank order 0, 1, 2, 3.
+
+Inputs must be dense contiguous CUDA tensors on the runtime's device, have at
+least one dimension and no empty dimensions, and have a row count divisible by
+four. Each quarter must contain a positive multiple of 16 bytes. Input and
+output addresses must be 16-byte aligned, and their memory ranges must not
+overlap. Output, when supplied, must exactly match the input shape and dtype.
+Physical tensor bytes are copied without arithmetic, dtype conversion or
+padding; unresolved conjugate/negative views and quantized tensors are rejected.
+The caller must submit matching shape/dtype and collective order on every rank.
+There is no per-operation host shape exchange or automatic fallback.
+
+The GPU stages the **complete input** in `send[seq & 1]`. The per-slot control
+byte count also describes that complete input. For destination `d`, the proxy
+reads from `send + d * (input_bytes/4)` and divides that quarter into two
+16-byte-aligned stripes. On the destination, source `s` writes to the start of
+`recv[s][seq & 1]`; the destination index is not added to the receive address.
+Each stripe is followed by its sequence flag on the same RC QP. Even a
+zero-length second stripe sends its flag. The kernel waits on all six flags,
+copies received quarters, and copies the local quarter from its rank offset.
+
+`API_VERSION = "mesh-owner-all-to-all-v1"` and native ABI `0x4F574E01` are
+distinct from serving RoCEnante. Constructor configuration votes and native
+connection-blob checks reject mixed runtime versions. The old all-reduce and
+all-gather entry points explicitly fail; this package cannot be used as an
+ordinary all-reduce/all-gather adapter.
+
+## Route and environment configuration
+
+All environment settings are isolated under `MESH_OWNER_`; `B12X_ROCE_*` and
+`NCCL_IB_*` do not select this runtime's devices, cache or scheduling.
+
+| Setting | Default and constraints |
+|---|---|
+| `MESH_OWNER_HCA` | `rocep1s0f0,rocep1s0f1,roceP2p1s0f0,roceP2p1s0f1`; exact order required |
+| `MESH_OWNER_GID_INDEX` | `3`; other values rejected |
+| `MESH_OWNER_PEER_HCA_MAP` | Rank-specific canonical map below; overrides must match it exactly |
+| `MESH_OWNER_OPPOSITE_PATHS` | `2`; four-path mode rejected |
+| `MESH_OWNER_WAVE_MODE` | `two`; also accepts `mixed2`, `opposite_first`, `strict3` |
+| `MESH_OWNER_TWO_WAVE_THRESHOLD_BYTES` | `131072`; zero disables scheduling, otherwise a multiple of 16 within uint32 |
+| `MESH_OWNER_SPIN_LIMIT` | `20000000` flag polls; positive uint32 |
+| `MESH_OWNER_CACHE_DIR` | `$XDG_CACHE_HOME/mesh_owner` or `~/.cache/mesh_owner` |
+| `CC` | Optional native C compiler; otherwise gcc, cc, clang |
+
+The wave threshold uses **bytes actually sent to one peer**, not the full
+input: the default threshold activates at a 512 KiB full input. All existing
+two-path wave ordering and completion drains are retained. Scheduling settings
+must agree across ranks.
+
+| Rank | Canonical `MESH_OWNER_PEER_HCA_MAP` |
+|---|---|
+| 0 | `1=0/2,2=0/3,3=1/3` |
+| 1 | `0=1/3,2=0/2,3=0/3` |
+| 2 | `0=1/2,1=1/3,3=0/2` |
+| 3 | `0=0/2,1=1/2,2=1/3` |
+
+Remote device/GID/QPN/MR/rkey comes from the reciprocal peer map and connection
+exchange. Only opposite-rank QPs retain flow label 16383; neighbor QPs retain
+zero. Managed fabric routes and markers must already exist.
+
+## Slots, streams and errors
+
+Only one kernel from a runtime may execute at a time. A lifecycle lock orders
+enqueueing; a CUDA event serializes different eager streams. Graph capture
+requires `prepare()` first and one stream per capture. Graph replays and eager
+operations using the same runtime must also be ordered by the caller. Callers
+must not mutate the input or consume the output until its stream dependency is
+satisfied. Raw-pointer launches record input/output allocator use on that stream.
+
+Two-slot safety follows from waiting for **every source on every operation**:
+
+- Sender `s` cannot reuse its send slot from operation N for N+2 until it
+  receives every peer's N+1 flags. Each peer starts N+1 only after receiving
+  `s`'s N flags, which follow the source DMA reads on the same ordered QPs.
+- Sender `s` cannot write N+2 into receiver `r`'s N slot until it receives
+  `r`'s N+1 flag. Receiver `r` publishes N+1 only after all its blocks finish
+  reading N and advance the epoch. Sender-local completions alone are not
+  used as receive credits.
+- A delayed proxy may miss at most two doorbells. It catches up in sequence
+  using the full input byte count saved per slot. More than two pending
+  doorbells is fatal. Quarter selection does not change these dependencies.
+
+The pinned layout deliberately retains full-size receive slots, preserving
+the existing offsets: total bytes are `10 * align_up(capacity,4096) + 2176`.
+A 32 MiB input capacity therefore allocates about 320 MiB pinned memory.
+
+Invalid local tensors fail before enqueueing. Configuration, native build,
+allocation and QP-creation failures are voted across the bootstrap group.
+A failed proxy raises its verbs/completion error. A kernel timeout records
+the failed sequence and source, poisons the runtime, and makes subsequent
+launches no-ops; `check_health()` raises. Work is asynchronous, so health
+checked immediately after enqueue cannot establish completion: synchronize
+the relevant stream before the final health check. This is also required after
+graph replay. Do not reuse a poisoned runtime or fall back rank-locally.
+`close()` synchronizes the device before releasing QPs and registrations.
+
+`stats()` reports epoch, control/error sequence, proxy operations/completions,
+path map and wave settings. `benchmark_counters()` reports six absolute
+origin-QP records with payload bytes, physical-hop payload bytes, flag writes,
+completions/errors, device and reciprocal QPN/HCA information. Standard verbs
+does not expose per-QP retry packet counts; those fields remain `None`.
+
+## Local validation and provenance
+
+Run from the parent directory:
+
+```text
+python -m compileall -q mesh_owner
+python -m unittest mesh_owner.test_layout -v
+```
+
+Four CPU tests pass. They cover input bounds, quarter and stripe intervals,
+zero-length stripe flags in a protocol model, canonical route configuration,
+and 32 randomized schedules of 80 operations across four ranks (10,240 rank
+exchanges), with varying per-operation sizes and actual two-doorbell catch-up.
+The model asserts both source lifetime and receiver consumption before slot
+reuse. These tests do not establish CUDA memory ordering or network routing;
+those require the separate four-rank hardware harness.
+
+Source was copied from the running B12X overlay at
+`/opt/spark-sircl/b12x_overlay/b12x/comm/roce` before isolated changes. Source
+archive: `../mesh-source.tar.gz`, SHA-256
+`a34ac1e86021a05ec565f6121a3b1053052169499b9d30b871871a849075ce11`.
+The reciprocal routing audit is in
+`outputs/glm53-owner-merge-20260907/transport-plan.md` in the workspace.
